_margin": -8.48, "analyst_adjustment": -1.52, "key_factors": ["District's R+8 partisan lean in an open seat", "Kingston's massive money advantage: $1.9M raised plus $1.9M outside support vs. Hollowell's $163K", "Unanimous expert ratings in the Safe/Solid/Likely R column and markets pricing Democrats near 7%", "No public general-election polling; 2026 environment tilts Republican"], "rationale": "The open seat retains a strong eight-point Republican lean, and Jim Kingston's overwhelming fundraising and outside-spending edge plus unanimous Safe-to-Likely R ratings justify moving slightly further toward the GOP than fundamentals alone. Amanda Hollowell's runoff win and Buttigieg endorsement show Democratic energy, but her thin war chest leaves little to contest the structural advantage.", "watch": "A national Democratic wave or unusually strong turnout around Savannah and the coast could pull the margin back toward single digits.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Buddy Carter (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Georgia's first district is an open Republican-held seat along the coast with a partisan lean of about eight points toward the GOP. Buddy Carter's retirement to run for Senate removes the incumbent advantage, but Republicans consolidated quickly: Jim Kingston dominated the primary field and enters the general with roughly $1.9 million raised plus about $1.9 million in outside support. Democrat Amanda Hollowell won a contested primary and runoff and earned a Pete Buttigieg endorsement, but has raised only about $163,000 with minimal cash on hand.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals. Expert raters unanimously place the race in the Safe, Solid, or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 7 percent chance. The district's structural lean and the money gap make Kingston a clear favorite, though open-seat dynamics leave some room for movement.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0834, "margin": -8.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.081, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0871, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0639, "margin": -10.0}]}